[00:17.70]property n. 所有物，财产；性质，特性 示例 ① Individuals and businesses have legal protection for intellectual property they create and own. 个人和企业创造和拥有的知识产权受法律保护。（2008. 12） ② The billionaire deeded his property to his daughter. 那个亿万富翁立契约把财产转让给女儿。
[00:23.57]stylish a. 时髦的，新潮的，高雅的 示例 ① Until the National Building Museum and Hill Country began hosting its Friday night barbecues with Hill Country, nothing signaled the arrival of summer in D.C. like thousands of stylish 20-and 30-somethings on the grass for the National Gallery of Art's weekly Jazz the Garden concerts. 在（华盛顿）国家建筑博物馆和（得克萨斯州）希尔县联合主办 “周五晚上来希尔县吃烧烤”活动之前，没有什么能比得上成千上万二三十岁时髦的年轻人在草地上参加国家艺术馆一周举办一次的爵士乐花园音乐会更能标志着夏天已经来到华盛顿。（The Washington Post） ② She usually likes wigs that are stylish, but not too outlandish. 她通常喜欢那种时髦但并不太古怪的假发。
[00:30.02]depress vt. 使压抑，使沮丧；使萧条 示例 ① Referring to a big story about Fortune's Most Powerful Women in Sunday's Washington Post, the Facebook COO asked if I'd been misquoted in saying that I believe women will never have 50% of the top jobs in corporate America. "Don't depress me!" Sandberg wrote. 桑德伯格是脸谱网的首席运营官。她 （在邮件中）提到，周日的《华盛顿邮报》 刊登了一篇关于《财富》“最具影响力女性” 榜单的大幅报道。报道中引用了我的一句话 ——女性在美国企业的高层职位中所占比例永远达不到50%。桑德伯格问我这句话是否是媒体搞错了。“别打击我！”她写道。（Fortune） ② Wet weather always depresses her. 阴雨天总使她心情抑郁。
[00:38.19]massive a. 巨大的；非常严重的 示例 ① It was a massive project, easily surpassing the scale of such previous human endeavors as the Panama Canal. 它（州际高速公路系统）是一个大规模的项目，远远超过早先人们建造巴拿马运河时的努力。（2009. 6）② I succeeded, but only after a massive effort. 我成功了，但是在付出了巨大的努力之后成功的。
[00:44.60]status n. 法律地位；身份；状况 示例 ① They earned just as much as graduates from higher-status schools. 他们的收入跟地位较高的学校的学生一样。（2008. 6）② They will change the status of the system. 他们将会改变这个系统的状态。
[00:52.08]veil n. 面纱；头巾；掩盖‖v. 戴面纱；遮掩 示例 ① The country's social injustices, human rights abuses and imperial aspirations are, it's suggested, being discreetly veiled from view. 有人暗示称， 发生在这个国家的社会不公、侵犯人权和这个国家对帝国的渴望正在被小心翼翼地掩盖起来。（The Guardian）② The young lady who wears a black veil looks very mysterious. 这位带黑面纱的年轻女士看起来很神秘。
[01:01.23]ascertain vt. 查明，弄清 示例 ① To fill that gap Kurt Gray of the University of Maryland, and Annie Knickman and Dan Wegner of Harvard University, conducted an experiment designed to ascertain just how people perceive those in a persistent vegetative state. 为了填补这项空白，马里兰州大学的库尔特•格雷与哈佛大学的丹•韦格纳和安妮• 尼克曼共同做了一个实验来研究人们是怎样看待植物人的。（The Economist） ② He does not need to ascertain that certain result. 他没有必要去查明那个确定的结果。
[01:08.24]moreover ad. 而且，此外 示例 ① Moreover, the amount a physician receives leans heavily toward medical or surgical procedures. 此外，医生的收入严重偏向医疗或外科手术。（2009. 12）② A talented musician, she was, moreover, a writer of some note. 她是一位有才华的音乐家，而且也是有些名望的作家。
[01:17.25]oppose v. 反对，抵制，阻挠 示例 ① In fact, every step of the way, as (usually) Democratic leaders have tried to introduce work-family balance measures into the law, business groups have been strongly opposed. 事实上，每一步举措都遭到商业团体的强烈反对，正如（通常情况下）民主党领导人试图将“平衡工作与家庭” 的措施纳入法律体系时所遭遇的那样。 （2010. 6） ② They threw all those that opposed them into prison. 他们把所有反对他们的人都送进了监狱。
[01:24.02]approach v. 接近；着手处理‖n. 方法；接近；路径 示例 ① The U.S. takes the opposite approach by emphasizing the specialist rather than the primary care physician. 美国却反其道而行，注重专科医生而非初级护理医师。（2009. 12） ② Summer is approaching. 夏天就要到了。
[01:29.34]multiply v. 乘；成倍增加；繁殖 示例 ① Advanced societies need economic growth to satisfy the multiplying wants of their citizens. 先进的社会需要经济增长来满足公民日益增长的需求。（2007. 6） ② Our problems have multiplied since last summer. 自去年夏天开始，我们的问题成倍增加。
[01:36.95]fund n. 基金；[pl.]资金‖v. 为…提供资金，拨款给 示例 ① Today, the European Union is creating a $580 billion fund to ward off sovereign collapse. 如今，欧盟正在建立一个5800亿美元的基金来防止主权崩溃。（2012. 6）② The hospital is trying to raise funds for a new machine. 这家医院正设法募集资金购买一台新机器。
[01:43.54]belief n. 相信；信念；信仰 示例 ① We also need to know whether our thoughts, beliefs and ideas are in line with those of other people. 我们也需要知道我们的思想、信仰、观点是不是和其他人的一致。（2012. 12） ② I admire his passionate belief in doing what he likes. 我佩服他对自己喜欢的事的坚定信念。
[01:51.41]warfare n. 战争；（群体、公司等之间的）竞争 示例 ① Nor is there any sign of the intergenerational warfare predicted in the 1990s. 20世纪90年代预测的代际战争也没有任何发生的迹象。（2010. 12） ② There are a lot of countries engaged in the warfare. 有很多国家参与了这场战争。
[01:58.81]forth ad. 向前； 离去 示例 ① The more they do online, using Google's search engine, watching videos on YouTube and so forth, the better for Google. 他们上网做的事情越多——用谷歌的搜索引擎或在YouTube上看视频等等—— 对谷歌越有利。（The Economist） ② We will set forth at midnight. 我们在午夜时出发。
[02:04.85]assemble v. 聚集；组装 示例 ① But the damage to skill and craftsmanship—what's needed to build a complex airliner or a tractor, or for a worker to move up from assembler to machinist to supervisor—went largely unnoticed. 然而，这一切对技能或手工艺的伤害在很大程度上却并未引起人们的注意， 这些技能是制造一架复杂的飞机或一台拖拉机，或者一个工人从装配工升为机械师、监督员所需要的。（2013. 6）② Many distinguished persons assembled in the party. 在那次聚会上许多知名人士聚集在一起。
[02:12.31]erupt v. （火山）爆发，喷出；突然发生；突然发出（尤指叫喊） 示例 ① In A.D. 63, Pompeii was seriously damaged by an earthquake, and the locals immediately went to work rebuilding in the same spot—until they were buried altogether by a volcano eruption 16 years later. 公元63年，庞培在一次地震中受到严重破坏，当地居民立即在同一地点重建了这座古城——直到16年后他们全都被火山喷发掩埋住了。（2007. 6）② The volcano may erupt at any time. 这座火山随时都有可能喷发。
[02:20.37]orient v. 朝向；确定方位 示例 ① For hundreds of millions of years, turtles have struggled out of the sea to lay their eggs on sandy beaches, long before there were nature documentaries to celebrate them, or GPS satellites and marine biologists to track them, or volunteers to hand-carry the hatchlings down to the water's edge lest they become disoriented by headlights and crawl towards a motel parking lot instead. 亿万年来，海龟挣扎着从大海中爬到沙滩上产卵。很久之前，没有自然纪录片为它们庆祝，没有GPS卫星和海洋生物学家追踪它们，也没有志愿者因为担心幼龟受到汽车前大灯的干扰迷失了方向爬到汽车旅馆的停车场而把它们捧回水边。（2009. 6）② It will take the freshmen a while to orient themselves in campus. 大一新生要花一段时间才能熟悉大学环境。
[02:27.58]transit n. 运输；经过‖v. 通过 示例 ① As late as the 1950s, a large percentage of the American public used mass transit. 一直到20世纪50年代，公共交通才成为大多数美国人的选择。（2008. 12）② They will transit the strait at night. 他们将在夜间通过那个海峡。
[02:34.64]corporate a. 公司的，法人的，共同的 示例 ① As corporate layoffs increased, that part has eroded. 随着公司解雇的增加，这一部分已经被削弱了。（2007. 6）② This company is concerned about its corporate image. 这家公司关心它自身的企业形象。
[02:41.33]crack n. 爆裂声；裂缝‖v. 破裂；发出爆裂声 示例 ① Three-year students get first crack at course registration. 三年级学生在课程选择方面享有优先权。（2012. 6）② The ice cracked the minute we stood on it. 我们刚一踏上冰面，冰面就裂开了。
[02:48.87]depart v. 离开；离职 示例 ① That would exacerbate the economic pain because the departing would lose access to both the single market and valuable regional-support funds. 退出国将失去单一市场的准入权以及宝贵的区域援助基金，从而使其经济困难更为深重。（The Economist）② She departed her job on November 15. 她于11 月15日离职。
[02:54.63]benefit n. 优势，益处‖v. 对某人有用；得益于… 示例 ① So you can see how being good in the inter-personal realm actually was a direct benefit, even for effectively pursuing a technical task. 所以你可以看到拥有良好的人际关系网确实会有直接的益处，即便是要高效地完成一项技术任务也是如此。（2013. 6）② Who exactly can benefit from this policy? 到底谁能从这项政策中获益呢？
[03:01.85]permanent a. 永久的，永恒的；（员工）终生的， 长期的 示例 ① Chris Mckay, a planetary scientist at NASA's Ames Research Center, believes that in 50 years we may find evidence of alien life in the ancient permanent frost of Mars or on other planets. 美国国家宇航局艾姆斯氏研究中心的星际科学家克里斯•麦凯认为，50年后我们能够在火星或其他行星古老的永久冰雪带中找到外星生命存在的证据。（2008. 6）② The accident has done permanent damage to her body. 那次事故对她的身体造成了永久性的伤害。
[03:07.28]resemble v. 看起来像，显得像 示例 ① Space Island Group is going to build a ring-shaped, rotating "commercial space infrastructure" that will resemble the Discovery spacecraft in the movie "2001: A Space Odyssey". 太空岛组织计划建造一个环形旋转的“商业太空基础结构”， 类似电影《2001：太空漫游》中的探索号宇宙飞船。（2006. 12）② He closely resembles his father. 他和他父亲长得很像。
[03:13.16]doubtful a. 怀疑的；不大可能的 示例 ① The woman is doubtful about newspaper stories. 这位女士对报纸上的故事表示怀疑。（2007. 6）② She is doubtful about changing her job. 她在犹豫要不要换工作。
[03:19.98]slice n. 薄片；部分‖v. 把…切成薄片；切 示例 ① NASA's new satellite is set to survey high-energy gamma rays across a broad swath, including a slice on the high end of that scale that has never before observed. 美国宇航局发射的新卫星将在一块广阔的地方测量高能伽马射线，还包括之前从未观测过的范围中数值高的一小片区域。（Scientific American）② The rent for my room is a large slice out of my expense. 房租是我开销中的一大部分。
[03:28.41]complain v. 抱怨，埋怨，发牢骚 示例 ① The Loews theater in Manhattan took the rare step of pulling the trailer from its screens after several complaints. 曼哈顿的洛斯剧场在接到几次投诉之后把该预告片撤掉了，而这是它极其少有的做法。（2008. 6） ② He works very hard and never complains about his work. 他工作非常努力，且从未抱怨过他的工作。
[03:35.08]heap n. 一堆；许多‖v. 堆积；在…上放很多 （东西） 示例 ① She also got heaps of praise for bucking the "helicopter parent" trend: "Good for this Mom," one commenter wrote on the Huffington Post. 她还因为反对“直升机父母”这一趋势而得到了很多赞扬，《赫芬顿邮报》上有评论者说：“这个妈妈不错。”（2009. 6） ② Rocks are heaped up on both sides of the road. 道路两边堆积着石头。
[03:42.30]inherent a. 固有的，内在的，难免的 示例 ① More than that, empathy as well as deep thought, depends on neural processes that are "inherently slow". 不止这些，同情和一些内心深处的想法一样，需要经过脑部加工的过程，这些过程从本质上说都是缓慢的。（2012. 6） ② Injustice is inherent in many countries. 在许多国家， 不公平待遇是难免的。
[03:49.65]source n. 来源；原始资料；起源；发源地‖v. 从…获得 示例 ① Starting in the 1980s, skill in finance grew in importance, and, as depicted in the news media and the movies, became a more appealing source of income. 从20世纪80年代开始，金融方面的技能变得越来越重要，而且正如新闻媒体和电影里所描绘的那样，这种技能已成为一种更具吸引力的收入来源。（2013. 6）② The library of your school will be a useful source of information. 你们学校的图书馆将成为有用的信息来源。
[03:57.84]prince n. 王子 示例 ① On the left Prince Josef Poniatowski rides forward in classical dress, like a supersized Marcus Aurelius. 左手边的是约瑟夫•波尼亚托夫斯基亲王，身穿古典长袍策马前行，看上去就好像是放大版的马克•奥勒。（The Economist） ② He is the prince of comedy. 他是喜剧大师。 语料 Ambition, in a private man a vice, is in a prince, a virtue. 野心，在平民身上是罪孽，在帝王身上却是美德。（英国剧作家马辛格）
[04:03.83]irritate v. 使烦恼；刺激 示例 ① I had an old aunt who used to throw cups of tea at people when she was particularly irritated. 我曾有一个年纪很大的姑姑，当她非常恼怒的时候经常将茶杯带茶水地抛向别人。（2011. 6）② His accent really irritates me. 他的口音实在令我恼火。
[04:09.01]overall a. 全面的，综合的‖ad. 全部，总计‖n. 外套，罩衣；工装服 示例 ① And Warren Buffett, the good-natured financier, became a homespun folk hero, without the tools and overalls. 温厚的金融家沃伦•巴菲特成了一名朴实的民间英雄，而他却不需要使用工具，也不用穿工作服。（2013. 6）② There is an overall improvement in standards of living. 人民的生活水平有整体的提高。
[04:17.14]overturn v. 倾倒，倾覆；推翻，撤销（判决等） 示例 ① The New York Times Company joined a brief filed by numerous organizations urging the Supreme Court to overturn the decision. 纽约时报公司加入了由众多组织提出的一起诉讼，敦促最高法院推翻这个决定。（The New York Times） ② The car hit on another one and overturned. 这辆车撞上了另一辆车，翻倒了。
[04:24.01]absence n. 缺席；不存在，缺乏 示例 ① Much of the concern among politicians about the state of American universities today is focused on the absence of "real world" education—which means preparation for professional and scientific careers. 政界人士对美国大学目前状态的关注大多都集中在“现实世界”教育的缺乏上面——所谓的“现实世界”教育即为专业和科学的职业做准备的教育。（2010. 12） ② The final decision was made in his absence. 这个最终决定是在他不在场的时候做出的。
[04:31.38]install v. 安装；建立（程序） 示例 ① Several countries have used subsidies to jump-start the market, including Japan, where almost 1 million heat pumps have been installed in the past two years to heat water for showers and hot tubs. 包括日本在内的一些国家已经通过发放补贴的方式启动这个市场，过去的两年间，日本已经安装了近100万台热水泵来加热淋浴和泡澡用水。（2007. 12）② The hotel has recently installed a new security system. 这家旅馆最近安装了新的安保系统。
[04:39.67]significant a. 有重大意义的；有某种意义的；意味深长的 示例 ① Leadership is the most significant word in today's competitive business environment because it directs the manager of a business to focus inward on their personal capabilities and style. （2011. 12）在当今竞争激烈的商业环境中，“领导才能”是最重要的字眼，因为它引导着公司管理层专注于发展其内在的个人能力和管理风格。② There are significant differences between the two groups of students. 这两组学生有明显差别。
[04:47.30]preserve v. 保护；保存；贮存；保全 示例 ① Malena Amusa, a 24-year-old writer and dancer from St. Louis sees the project as a way to preserve history as it happens. 来自圣•路易斯的24岁作家、舞者玛丽娜•阿姆撒认为这个工程可以很好地保存史实。（2010. 6）② The antique has been preserved intact. 这个古董保存得完好无损。
[04:53.60]downfall n. 衰败；垮台；衰落（或衰败、垮台） 的原因 示例 ① These have already led to the arrest of several bankers and to the downfall of the Bank of Italy's governor, Antonio Fazio. 这些已经导致几位银行家锒铛入狱以及意大利银行行长安东尼奥•法齐奥的下台。（The Economist） ② The scandal leads to his downfall. 丑闻让他身败名裂。
